88 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 66 0 R
/E (This project presents Can I Hinder? a crowd-interactive 2.5 action adventure game that explores the integration of real time spectator input into a traditionally single-player experience. The system is built across multiple components, including a C++ SFML game client, a WebSocket relay server, A REST API and a Progressive Web App \(PWA\), all working together to create a live, reactive gameplay environment.)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
89 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 66 0 R
/E (The core Idea behind this project is to introduce unpredictability and emergent behaviour through audience participation. Spectators are able to influence game play in real-time by choosing to either assist the player through buffs or hinder their progress through debuffs and environmental challenges. This transforms the experience from a static single-player journey into a dynamic system shaped by both the player and the audience.)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [10]
>>
endobj
90 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 66 0 R
/E (This project demonstrates how real-time networking and modern web technologies can be combined with game design to create engaging and interactive experiences. It also highlights the technical and design challenges involved in synchronising multiple systems, maintaining performance and balancing player control with external influences.)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [11]
>>
endobj
91 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /Figure
/P 67 0 R
/Pg 11 0 R
/A [303 0 R 0]
/K [0]
>>
