>>
endobj
93 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 67 0 R
/E (The central question behind this project is whether real-time audience interaction can meaningfully enhance a single player experience. Traditional action-adventure games typically follow a structured and predictable design, where the player progresses through challenges with limited external influence. While this allows for controlled gameplay, it often lacks the unpredictability and variation seen in live, shared experiences.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
94 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 67 0 R
/E (Can I Hinder? was developed to explore how this model can be extended by introducing a live spectator interaction layer. By allowing external participants to connect to the game through a web-based interface and influence gameplay in real-time, the project aims to transform a single-player experience into a dynamic shared system.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
95 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 67 0 R
/E (This project was motivated by the growing popularity of live-streamed gameplay and interactive media, where audiences are no longer passive viewers but active contributors. Platforms that support real-time interaction have demonstrated that audience partcipation can significantly shaper player experience, but integrating this into a structured game environment presents both technical and design challenges.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
96 0 obj
<<
