/S /P
/P 67 0 R
/E (The primary research question explored in this project is:)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
97 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 67 0 R
/T (Can real-time spectator interaction, enhance player engagement and introduce meaningful variation in a single player action-adventure game?)
/E (Can real-time spectator interaction, enhance player engagement and introduce meaningful variation in a single player action-adventure game?)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
98 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 67 0 R
/E (To address this question, the project aims to design and implement a fully playable game supported by a multi-component architecture, while also exploring how such a system can be balanced to ensure that spectator influence enhances, rather than disrupts, the core gameplay experience.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
