126 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 70 0 R
/E (This solution significantly improved the reliability of enemy spawning and ensured that enemies appeared in valid and accessible positions. However, it also highlighted the importance of validating gameplay logic against environment data, particularly when working with tile-based maps and dynamic spawning systems.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
127 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 71 0 R
/E (Another notable issue was deploying to Azure, particularly when trying to update existing services. Initally, deployment was handled through VS Code, however updates to both  the PWA and Node server were not consistently applied. This meant that even after deploying changes, the live version would not reflect the latest code. As a result, the only reliable workaround at the time was to delete and redeploy the services, which slowed down development significantly.)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [0]
>>
endobj
128 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 71 0 R
/E (To resolve this, I implemented a continous deployment pipeline using GitHub Actions. YAML workflows were created for the PWA, Node.js and the API, using Azure publish profiles stored as Github secrets. This allowed the project to automatically build and deploy whenever changes were pushed to the main branch.)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
129 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 71 0 R
/E (This approach made deployment far more reliable and removed the need for manual redeployment.)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
130 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 71 0 R
/E (One of the main things that went right in the project was the integration of multiple systems into a single working application. The game client, WebSocket relay server, REST API, and PWA were all able to communicate together in real time. Seeing everything connect and work together for the first time was incredibly satisfying, as this was the core goal of the project.)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
131 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 71 0 R
/E (The help and hinder unlock system also worked very well once implemented. It created a stronger incentive for spectators to stay engaged, giving them a reason to continue interacting with the game rather than just sending occasional inputs.)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
132 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 71 0 R
/E (As discussed above, the deployment pipeline using GitHub Actions made deployment much faster and more reliable. This allowed more time to be spent on developing the game itself rather than dealing with deployment issues.)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
133 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 71 0 R
/E (The introduction of the turn-based battle system is one of the biggest highlights of the project. It not only adds variety to the gameplay, but also challenged me to think more carefully about balancing. Managing different abilities, magic effects, and items made this part of development particularly enjoyable and rewarding.)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
